我想知道编剧室里是谁想出了“邪恶的蜗牛”这个词，因为太搞笑了。

1141
00:46:30.940 --> 00:46:33.000
It's such a good description of Toby.
对托比的形容太贴切了。

1142
00:46:33.280 --> 00:46:34.040
Such a good description.
形容得太贴切了。

1143
00:46:34.300 --> 00:46:37.600
And then he goes on to say he feels like Neve Campbell in Scream 2, and he has this very
接着他说他觉得自己就像《惊声尖叫2》里的内芙·坎贝尔，他还有一段

1144
00:46:37.600 --> 00:46:40.860
funny talking head where he learned a lot, I guess, from the Scream movies.
非常搞笑的单人访谈，我猜他是从《惊声尖叫》系列电影里学到了很多。

1145
00:46:41.440 --> 00:46:44.660
But Jenna, there was another talking head in the script.
但是珍娜，剧本里还有另一段单人访谈。

1146
00:46:44.660 --> 00:46:49.140
So the one you see with the Neve Campbell, that was not in the script.
所以你们看到的那个关于内芙·坎贝尔的，并没有在剧本里。

1147
00:46:49.380 --> 00:46:52.620
So that must have been an alternate talking head they handed him on the day.
那肯定是在拍摄当天临时塞给他的备用单人访谈。

1148
00:46:52.780 --> 00:46:53.200
Okay.
好吧。

1149
00:46:53.820 --> 00:46:56.140
In the script, this is Michael's talking head.
在剧本里，这是迈克尔的单人访谈。

1150
00:46:56.300 --> 00:46:58.900
It's almost the same right up until the evil snail.
几乎一模一样，一直到“邪恶的蜗牛”那部分。

1151
00:46:58.900 --> 00:47:01.320
So evil snail was in the script.
所以剧本里有邪恶蜗牛。

1152
00:47:01.780 --> 00:47:02.260
Yes.
是的。

1153
00:47:02.440 --> 00:47:03.900
Evil snail was a keeper.
邪恶蜗牛是个保留节目。

1154
00:47:04.180 --> 00:47:05.320
We've always had that.
我们一直都有这个。

1155
00:47:05.520 --> 00:47:07.580
But this is how it changed in the script.
但剧本里是这样改的。

1156
00:47:07.840 --> 00:47:11.460
The last four months without Toby have been absolute bliss.
没有托比的过去四个月简直是人间仙境。

1157
00:47:11.820 --> 00:47:14.020
I fell in love with a beautiful blonde woman.
我爱上了一位美丽的金发女郎。

1158
00:47:14.220 --> 00:47:15.340
I fell out of love.
我又失恋了。

1159
00:47:15.480 --> 00:47:16.500
I tried scallops.
我尝了扇贝。

1160
00:47:16.640 --> 00:47:18.060
The office was broken into.
办公室遭窃了。

1161
00:47:18.260 --> 00:47:19.080
I became a father.
我当爸爸了。

1162
00:47:19.260 --> 00:47:20.140
I grew a goatee.
我留了山羊胡。

1163
00:47:20.380 --> 00:47:22.580
The Olympics were a great success for China.
奥运会为中国取得了巨大成功。

1164
00:47:22.760 --> 00:47:25.460
And now that I've tasted freedom, I can never go back.
既然我尝过了自由的滋味，就再也回不去了。

1165
00:47:25.660 --> 00:47:26.960
I'm going to kill him.
我要杀了他。

1166
00:47:26.960 --> 00:47:28.140
No, too far.
不行，有点过火。

1167
00:47:28.320 --> 00:47:29.320
But I will do something.
但我会做点什么。

1168
00:47:29.500 --> 00:47:30.000
No, too little.
不行，力度不够。

1169
00:47:30.140 --> 00:47:31.120
I will get rid of him.
我要除掉他。

1170
00:47:31.480 --> 00:47:32.480
Oh, I like it.
哦，我喜欢这个。

1171
00:47:32.680 --> 00:47:34.820
I love his breakdown of what all happened.
我喜欢他对发生的事情的总结。

1172
00:47:34.820 --> 00:47:37.160
And I love that he included he grew a goatee.
我也喜欢他把留山羊胡也算进去了。

1173
00:47:39.710 --> 00:47:40.430
Me too.
我也是。

1174
00:47:41.050 --> 00:47:45.910
It's true, in fact, that Michael is going to try to get rid of Toby.
事实上，迈克尔确实打算除掉托比。

1175
00:47:46.290 --> 00:47:48.810
He is looking for fireable offenses.
他在寻找能被开除的过错。

1176
00:47:49.690 --> 00:47:52.310
Dwight says there are two that he can find in this binder.
德怀特说他在这个文件夹里找到了两条。

1177
00:47:53.110 --> 00:47:55.390
Workplace violence or sexual harassment.
职场暴力或性骚扰。

1178
00:47:55.390 --> 00:48:01.530
So I guess Michael's first plan is to try to get Toby to sexually harass Pam.
所以我想迈克尔的第一个计划是试图让托比性骚扰帕姆。

1179
00:48:01.930 --> 00:48:03.610
He goes up to Pam's desk.
他走到帕姆的桌子前。

1180
00:48:03.810 --> 00:48:05.250
He hands Pam a note.
他递给帕姆一张便条。

1181
00:48:05.590 --> 00:48:08.390
And he says, go give this note to Toby.
他说，把这张便条拿给托比。

1182
00:48:08.630 --> 00:48:09.250
Don't read it.
别看。

1183
00:48:09.450 --> 00:48:10.090
Don't read it.
别看。

1184
00:48:10.730 --> 00:48:11.810
Pam reads it.
帕姆看了。

1185
00:48:12.790 --> 00:48:15.870
In the note, it's written as if it's from Pam.
便条上的语气写得像是帕姆写的。

1186
00:48:16.090 --> 00:48:18.190
And it says, please hug and kiss me.
上面写着，请抱抱我，亲亲我。

1187
00:48:18.290 --> 00:48:21.870
No matter how much I struggle, I'm too shy to confess my love to you.
不管我怎么挣扎，我都太害羞了，不敢向你表白。

1188
00:48:21.870 --> 00:48:25.010
So can you imagine if Toby had read that note?
所以你能想象如果托比读了那张便条会怎样吗？

1189
00:48:25.370 --> 00:48:26.850
His brain would have exploded.
他的大脑会炸掉的。

1190
00:48:27.310 --> 00:48:27.750
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1191
00:48:28.190 --> 00:48:28.470
Yeah.
对。

1192
00:48:28.790 --> 00:48:30.150
Well, that doesn't work.
好吧，这行不通。

1193
00:48:30.610 --> 00:48:30.770
Yeah.
对。

1194
00:48:31.050 --> 00:48:33.210
Pam's like, no, I'm not going back there.
帕姆一副“不，我才不回去呢”的表情。

1195
00:48:33.430 --> 00:48:39.230
So now the new plan is to get Toby to beat up Michael.
所以现在的新计划是让托比痛扁迈克尔一顿。

1196
00:48:39.610 --> 00:48:39.950
Yeah.
对。

1197
00:48:40.090 --> 00:48:41.570
So they march back to the annex.
于是他们气势汹汹地朝套间走去。

1198
00:48:41.810 --> 00:48:47.710
And Michael's sort of confronting Toby and trying to sort of, you know, antagonize him to hit him.
迈克尔有点在质问托比，并试图，你知道的，挑衅他动手打人。

1199
00:48:47.830 --> 00:48:48.790
And Dwight's like, hit him.
德怀特在一旁说，打他。

1200
00:48:48.790 --> 00:48:50.650
And then Kelly jumps in so quickly.
然后凯莉反应极快地插话了。

1201
00:48:50.810 --> 00:48:51.290
Hit him.
揍他。

1202
00:48:51.590 --> 00:48:52.130
I know.
我知道。

1203
00:48:52.270 --> 00:48:54.210
First of all, her and Ryan were making out.
首先，她和瑞安在亲热。

1204
00:48:54.430 --> 00:48:54.990
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1205
00:48:55.150 --> 00:48:57.970
That they've stopped making out so that they can weigh in.
他们现在停下来好发表意见。

1206
00:48:58.110 --> 00:48:59.410
And they're for a fight.
而且他们支持打架。

1207
00:48:59.610 --> 00:49:00.530
They're like, do it.
他们就像是在说，上吧。

1208
00:49:00.770 --> 00:49:01.250
Hit him.
揍他。

1209
00:49:01.530 --> 00:49:01.970
Hit him.
揍他。

1210
00:49:02.470 --> 00:49:03.270
Toby refuses.
托比拒绝了。

1211
00:49:03.790 --> 00:49:04.750
It's not working.
这招没用。

1212
00:49:05.290 --> 00:49:06.530
None of these plans are working.
这些计划全都没用。

1213
00:49:06.990 --> 00:49:08.690
So you know what they're going to have to do?
所以你知道他们打算怎么做吗？

1214
00:49:09.030 --> 00:49:10.310
They're going to have to go big.
他们打算玩个大的。

1215
00:49:10.590 --> 00:49:13.550
They're going to have to frame Toby for drugs.
他们打算栽赃托比吸毒。

1216
00:49:14.110 --> 00:49:15.130
Like on the shield.
就像《盾牌》里那样。

1217
00:49:15.130 --> 00:49:18.050
I love that Dwight said, I've framed many animals.
我喜欢德怀特说的话：我陷害过很多动物。

1218
00:49:19.410 --> 00:49:22.010
I framed a raccoon opening a Christmas gift.
我陷害过一只正在拆圣诞礼物的浣熊。

1219
00:49:22.850 --> 00:49:23.910
Oh, Dwight.
哦，德怀特。

1220
00:49:24.570 --> 00:49:30.050
Well, Michael thinks it sounds mean, but sometimes the end justifies the mean.
好吧，迈克尔觉得这听起来很卑鄙，但有时目的正当可以不择手段。

1221
00:49:30.230 --> 00:49:31.490
That's such a good line.
这台词写得真好。

1222
00:49:31.750 --> 00:49:32.750
It's such a good line.
这台词写得太棒了。

1223
00:49:32.750 --> 00:49:34.010
It's so smart.
太聪明了。

1224
00:49:34.270 --> 00:49:35.410
It's smart money.
这才是聪明人的做法。

1225
00:49:35.770 --> 00:49:38.190
It reminds me of this gem.
这让我想起了这个名场面。

1226
00:49:38.470 --> 00:49:41.430
I'm not superstitious, but I'm a little bit stitious.
我虽然不迷信，但我有点迷信。

1227
00:49:41.750 --> 00:49:42.230
Yes.
没错。

1228
00:49:42.230 --> 00:49:44.610
That it's right in line with that.
这完全符合那种风格。

1229
00:49:45.170 --> 00:49:51.390
So yeah, Michael's going to go and hit up Leo and Gino over in Vance Refrigeration for some drugs.
所以没错，迈克尔去找万斯冷气公司的利奥和吉诺搞点毒品。

1230
00:49:51.670 --> 00:49:56.010
They give him what they say is two pounds of weed and they want $500.
他们给了他据称是两磅的大麻，并索要五百美元。

1231
00:49:56.770 --> 00:49:59.650
Michael has $500 in his wallet?
迈克尔钱包里有五百美元？

1232
00:50:00.110 --> 00:50:01.570
I thought the same thing.
我也这么想。

1233
00:50:02.010 --> 00:50:03.950
That's a lot of cash in your wallet.
钱包里带着这么多现金。

1234
00:50:04.290 --> 00:50:09.130
And for my background catch people, did you see the Lackawanna library card?
对于注意背景细节的观众，你们看到拉克瓦纳图书馆的借书卡了吗？

1235
00:50:09.130 --> 00:50:10.790
In Michael's wallet?
在迈克尔的钱包里？

1236
00:50:11.130 --> 00:50:11.650
Yes.
对。

1237
00:50:11.770 --> 00:50:15.710
When he opens his wallet, there's a Lackawanna County Library card.
当他打开钱包时，里面有一张拉克瓦纳县图书馆的借书卡。

1238
00:50:15.990 --> 00:50:18.870
Do you know what I found recently when I was cleaning out my closet?
你知道我最近打扫衣柜时发现了什么吗？

1239
00:50:19.250 --> 00:50:19.770
What?
什么？

1240
00:50:20.130 --> 00:50:21.030
Pam's wallet.
帕姆的钱包。

1241
00:50:21.330 --> 00:50:22.190
You did.
真的吗。

1242
00:50:22.470 --> 00:50:26.950
And in it, there's a credit card that says Pam Beasley.
里面有一张写着帕姆·比斯利的信用卡。

1243
00:50:27.270 --> 00:50:31.650
There's all these cards they made for my wallet, my prop wallet.
他们为我的钱包制作了所有这些卡片，也就是我的道具钱包。

1244
00:50:31.910 --> 00:50:32.730
I'll take a picture.
我会拍张照片。

1245
00:50:32.850 --> 00:50:33.770
We'll put it in pod.
我们把它发到播客里。

1246
00:50:34.010 --> 00:50:35.390
Yeah, we have to put it in stories.
对，我们得发到快拍里。

1247
00:50:35.430 --> 00:50:36.410
That's so fun.
太有意思了。

1248
00:50:36.590 --> 00:50:37.690
How crazy is that?
是不是太疯狂了？

1249
00:50:37.690 --> 00:50:38.450
They did that.
他们居然做了这个。

1250
00:50:38.590 --> 00:50:40.810
That's how detailed Phil Shea was.
菲尔·希a就是这么注重细节。

1251
00:50:40.950 --> 00:50:41.090
Yep.
对。

1252
00:50:41.310 --> 00:50:44.590
If you had a prop wallet, it reflected your character.
如果你有一个道具钱包，它能反映你的角色性格。

1253
00:50:45.130 --> 00:50:48.450
Although, is Michael going to the library and why?
不过，迈克尔去图书馆是去干嘛的，为什么去？

1254
00:50:48.610 --> 00:50:49.390
What's that for?
那是干什么用的？

1255
00:50:49.830 --> 00:50:55.410
I mean, I feel like Michael's probably had that library card for like 20 years in his wallet.
我的意思是，我觉得迈克尔钱包里的那张借书证大概用了二十年了。

1256
00:50:55.970 --> 00:50:56.150
Yeah.
是啊。

1257
00:50:56.530 --> 00:50:59.850
Maybe there was a time where he didn't have internet and he'd have to go to the library.
也许以前他没有网络，不得不去图书馆。

1258
00:51:00.110 --> 00:51:01.550
Oh, wait, we didn't have internet.
哦，等等，我们以前确实没有网络。

1259
00:51:02.470 --> 00:51:03.230
I know.
我知道。

1260
00:51:03.230 --> 00:51:08.370
Maybe he used to go to the library to make copies because the copier in the office is crap.
也许他以前去图书馆复印，因为办公室的复印机太烂了。

1261
00:51:08.610 --> 00:51:10.070
We'll get to that next week.
我们下周再聊这个。

1262
00:51:10.630 --> 00:51:10.830
Yeah.
对。

1263
00:51:11.470 --> 00:51:18.750
So, Ange, you know how when sometimes we're watching an episode or we're breaking down our document to prep to do the podcast,
所以，安吉，你知道有时候我们在看剧，或者在整理资料准备做播客时，

1264
00:51:18.750 --> 00:51:21.610
we'll get curious about something and we'll do a deep dive?
我们会对某个事情产生好奇，然后去深入研究一番吗？

1265
00:51:21.850 --> 00:51:23.170
Did you do one on something?
你针对什么事做过研究吗？

1266
00:51:23.410 --> 00:51:24.430
I didn't.
我没有。

1267
00:51:24.430 --> 00:51:26.690
Our associate producer, Ainsley.
我们的助理制片人，艾恩斯利。

1268
00:51:26.990 --> 00:51:28.530
Ainsley, what'd you deep dive?
艾恩斯利，你深入研究了什么？

1269
00:51:29.470 --> 00:51:31.130
This is what she wrote me.
这是她写给我的。

1270
00:51:31.430 --> 00:51:45.010
She said, according to a regrettable Google search, the price of one pound of recreational marijuana in Pennsylvania ranges from $1,900 to $2,550.
她说，根据一次让人哭笑不得的谷歌搜索，在宾夕法尼亚州，一磅消遣用大麻的价格从1900美元到2550美元不等。

1271
00:51:45.810 --> 00:51:47.070
She had to know.
她非得弄清楚不可。

1272
00:51:47.230 --> 00:51:51.170
She was like, okay, they're selling Michael two pounds of weed for $500.
她当时就想，好吧，他们以500美元的价格卖给迈克尔两磅大麻。

1273
00:51:51.970 --> 00:51:56.170
Ainsley got curious, how much is a pound of weed in Pennsylvania?
艾恩斯利很好奇，在宾夕法尼亚州一磅大麻多少钱？

1274
00:51:56.550 --> 00:52:00.170
And now, I looked and we shot this in September of 2008.
然后，我查了一下，我们是在2008年9月拍的这一集。

1275
00:52:00.170 --> 00:52:02.310
So, how much was it in 2008?
那么，在2008年它值多少钱呢？

1276
00:52:02.610 --> 00:52:07.110
I'm not sure, but today, that's going to run you quite a bit of money.
我不太确定，但放到现在，那可得花不少钱。

1277
00:52:07.590 --> 00:52:14.670
With today's prices, Michael got a deal because it would cost him close to $5,000 to get two pounds of weed today.
以目前的价格来看，迈克尔算是捡了个大便宜，因为如果要买两磅大麻，现在得花将近5000美元。

1278
00:52:14.950 --> 00:52:20.190
I also want to say that's clearly not two pounds of anything in that baggie.
我还想说，那个小袋子里装的明显不是两磅任何东西。

1279
00:52:20.190 --> 00:52:20.910
No.
没错。

1280
00:52:21.430 --> 00:52:23.910
It's green, but it's not two pounds.
它是绿色的，但绝对没有两磅重。

1281
00:52:24.210 --> 00:52:25.330
I mean, two pounds.
我是说，两磅。

1282
00:52:25.470 --> 00:52:30.510
I have two pounds of things all over my house, like two-pound weights, two-pound bag of flour.
我家里到处都是两磅重的东西，比如两磅重的哑铃、两磅重的面粉袋。

1283
00:52:30.710 --> 00:52:32.810
That's not two pounds of anything.
那绝对不是两磅重的任何东西。

1284
00:52:33.490 --> 00:52:34.230
It's not.
确实不是。

1285
00:52:34.430 --> 00:52:37.130
I've had a two-pound bag of spinach in my house before.
我以前在家里买过两磅重的菠菜。

1286
00:52:37.210 --> 00:52:38.510
It's much bigger than that.
比那个大得多。

1287
00:52:38.510 --> 00:52:40.010
It takes up the whole CRISPR drawer.
它占满整个保鲜抽屉。

1288
00:52:40.230 --> 00:52:45.590
You're very passionate about painting a very clear picture of what two pounds is.
你对清楚描绘两磅到底有多大非常有热情。

1289
00:52:45.590 --> 00:52:49.630
I mean, it's so glaringly obvious that that's not two pounds.
我是说，那根本不是两磅，简直显而易见。

1290
00:52:49.790 --> 00:52:52.090
There are so many signs that Michael is missing.
迈克尔错过了太多的迹象。

1291
00:52:52.370 --> 00:52:53.730
Don't get Jenna started.
别让珍娜打开话匣子。

1292
00:52:54.050 --> 00:52:57.110
Don't get me started on what two pounds of something is.
别让我开始唠叨两磅东西到底有多大。

1293
00:52:57.290 --> 00:52:59.670
I'll tell you about my two pounds of spinach.
我跟你讲讲我那两磅重的菠菜。

1294
00:52:59.990 --> 00:53:04.970
I just ordered two pounds of Epsom salts, and that was a large package as well.
我刚订购了两磅的泻盐，那也是很大一包。

1295
00:53:05.250 --> 00:53:06.210
What are you making?
你在做什么？

1296
00:53:06.490 --> 00:53:07.830
Warm, soothing bath.
温暖舒缓的泡澡。

1297
00:53:10.050 --> 00:53:15.050
Well, listen, we're about to find out that Pam has an ally in this whole microwave business.
好吧，听着，我们马上就会发现帕姆在这起微波炉事件中找到了一个盟友。

1298
00:53:15.650 --> 00:53:16.370
Does she?
是吗？

1299
00:53:16.570 --> 00:53:21.730
She has Ryan, who's pretending to be an ally, and he's laying it on thick, and I love it.
她有瑞安，他在假装盟友，而且表现得非常刻意，我太喜欢了。

1300
00:53:22.250 --> 00:53:24.250
Yeah, he says, I'm totally on your side.
对，他说，我完全站在你这边。

1301
00:53:24.310 --> 00:53:28.350
But the truth is, he went to make a cup of noodles, and the microwave is still a mess.
但事实是，他去泡了一杯面，而微波炉现在还是一团糟。

1302
00:53:28.490 --> 00:53:29.910
And he wants her to clean it up.
而且他想让帕姆去收拾。

1303
00:53:30.050 --> 00:53:32.550
And she delivers some real Pam sass.
接着她展现了真正的帕姆式毒舌。

1304
00:53:33.190 --> 00:53:38.670
Hey, Pam, I just want to let you know, I'm totally on your side with the whole microwave situation.
嘿，帕姆，我只想让你知道，关于微波炉这事，我完全站在你这边。

1305
00:53:39.630 --> 00:53:40.250
Thank you.
谢谢。

1306
00:53:40.430 --> 00:53:42.350
I was just back there to make some cup of soup.
我刚才去后面泡个汤来着。

1307
00:53:42.510 --> 00:53:43.850
The thing is still a huge mess.
那玩意儿现在还是一团大乱。

1308
00:53:43.970 --> 00:53:44.930
I know, can you believe it?
我知道，你敢信吗？

1309
00:53:45.070 --> 00:53:46.290
Yeah, it's crazy.
对啊，太离谱了。

1310
00:53:47.370 --> 00:53:53.950
But I guess the thing is, at some point, notes or no notes, someone's going to have to just get in there and clean it up.
但我想说的是，总得有人不管有没有便条，自己进去把它收拾干净才行。

1311
00:53:56.100 --> 00:53:57.740
I guess that's why we have a temp, huh?
我猜这就是为什么我们有个临时工，对吧？

1312
00:54:00.320 --> 00:54:02.800
Oh, no, trust me, I would just make it worse.
哦，不，相信我，我只会越弄越糟。

1313
00:54:02.800 --> 00:54:05.020
How would wiping it with a paper towel make it worse?
拿纸巾擦一下怎么会越弄越糟？

1314
00:54:05.080 --> 00:54:05.940
I would find a way.
我总有办法的。

1315
00:54:06.720 --> 00:54:08.400
You've seen things clean before, though, right?
不过你以前总见过别人打扫卫生吧？

1316
00:54:08.740 --> 00:54:10.360
Pam, I'm hopeless at that stuff.
帕姆，我对那种事一窍不通。

1317
00:54:10.640 --> 00:54:14.880
I mean, that's some good Pam sass.
我是说，这可真有点帕姆式的毒舌。

1318
00:54:15.100 --> 00:54:16.220
That was all scripted.
那全都是按剧本演的。

1319
00:54:16.340 --> 00:54:18.360
I know it sounds like Jenna sass.
我知道听起来像是珍娜式的毒舌。

1320
00:54:18.560 --> 00:54:19.440
It was scripted.
那是剧本里写的。

1321
00:54:19.540 --> 00:54:21.200
I just brought myself to it.
我只是把真情实感带进去了。

1322
00:54:21.360 --> 00:54:23.080
You brought some real truth to it.
你确实带入了一些大实话。

1323
00:54:23.120 --> 00:54:23.520
I did.
我是带了。

1324
00:54:24.200 --> 00:54:29.980
Well, Ange, we got a lot of fan questions asking, who did clean the microwave?
好了，安吉，我们收到了很多粉丝提问：到底是谁清理的微波炉？

1325
00:54:30.480 --> 00:54:32.400
Because this never gets wrapped up.
因为这件事一直没个交待。

1326
00:54:32.400 --> 00:54:33.540
We never find out.
我们始终没找出来。

1327
00:54:33.720 --> 00:54:34.800
Did it get clean?
到底洗干净了吗？

1328
00:54:34.940 --> 00:54:35.600
Who cleaned it?
是谁清理的？

1329
00:54:35.980 --> 00:54:37.680
This would have wrapped up.
本来这事应该有个结尾的。

1330
00:54:37.820 --> 00:54:38.840
It's in the script.
剧本里是有的。

1331
00:54:39.020 --> 00:54:41.960
And we filmed a big scene that would have explained all of it.
而且我们拍了一场能解释这一切的大戏。

1332
00:54:42.080 --> 00:54:43.740
It was a fun scene, too.
那也是一场很有意思的戏。

1333
00:54:44.180 --> 00:54:44.880
It was.
确实是的。

1334
00:54:44.880 --> 00:54:48.040
And it has a great Pam Angela moment at the top.
开头还有一个超棒的帕姆和安吉拉的互动时刻。

1335
00:54:48.300 --> 00:54:48.640
Yeah.
对。

1336
00:54:48.840 --> 00:54:50.400
So it starts with Angela.
所以是以安吉拉开场的。

1337
00:54:50.600 --> 00:54:52.020
She's storming in from the kitchen.
她气冲冲地从厨房走进来。

1338
00:54:52.180 --> 00:54:53.720
She's super ticked off.
她气炸了。

1339
00:54:53.780 --> 00:54:55.240
And she's holding up a note.
而且她举着一张便条。

1340
00:54:55.480 --> 00:54:59.000
Someone has drawn a penis on the note.
有人在那张便条上画了个生殖器。

1341
00:54:59.000 --> 00:55:00.160
And she confronts Pam.
然后她去找帕姆对质。

1342
00:55:00.480 --> 00:55:00.920
I know.
我知道。

1343
00:55:01.020 --> 00:55:02.620
She thinks Pam drew the penis.
她以为是帕姆画的。

1344
00:55:03.380 --> 00:55:06.820
Why does she always blame Pam for this kind of stuff?
为什么她老是把这种事怪在帕姆头上？

1345
00:55:06.960 --> 00:55:07.720
I don't know.
我不知道。

1346
00:55:07.960 --> 00:55:08.900
Here's how it went.
当时情况是这样的。

1347
00:55:10.180 --> 00:55:10.640
Pervert.
变态。

1348
00:55:12.240 --> 00:55:13.480
Angela, I didn't do that.
安吉拉，我没做过这事。

1349
00:55:13.640 --> 00:55:15.860
So is this what they taught you at your fancy art school?
所以这就是你在那个高级艺术学校学到的东西？

1350
00:55:15.860 --> 00:55:17.600
Why would I draw a penis on my own note?
我为什么要在自己的便条上画生殖器？

1351
00:55:17.900 --> 00:55:19.300
Why do you wear bright colors?
你为什么穿这么鲜艳的颜色？

1352
00:55:19.480 --> 00:55:20.260
For attention, Pam.
为了引人注目，帕姆。

1353
00:55:22.540 --> 00:55:24.640
Everyone, I have an announcement to make.
各位，我有件事要宣布。

1354
00:55:26.380 --> 00:55:28.940
I'm the person who put the first note on the microwave.
我就是那个在微波炉上贴第一张便条的人。

1355
00:55:30.380 --> 00:55:30.860
Yeah.
没错。

1356
00:55:31.200 --> 00:55:32.160
Pam comes clean.
帕姆坦白了。

1357
00:55:32.600 --> 00:55:37.700
And I remember shooting this because Pam kind of goes on to take charge of the room.
我记得拍这场戏的时候，因为帕姆有点开始掌控全场了。

1358
00:55:37.880 --> 00:55:40.940
After she admits that she wrote the note, she's like,
在她承认便条是她写之后，她就说，

1359
00:55:40.940 --> 00:55:45.460
and I guess I just have to say, what's so wrong about the note?
我想我不得不说，那张便条有什么不对的？

1360
00:55:45.600 --> 00:55:48.380
Why is everyone so offended by this note?
为什么大家对这张便条这么生气？

1361
00:55:48.560 --> 00:55:52.220
Shouldn't you be more offended by a consistently dirty microwave?
难道你们不应该对一直很脏的微波炉更生气吗？

1362
00:55:52.600 --> 00:55:54.220
She gets on her soapbox.
她开始发表长篇大论了。

1363
00:55:54.380 --> 00:55:55.600
It's Pam's soapbox.
这是帕姆的慷慨陈词。

1364
00:55:55.680 --> 00:55:56.920
It's Pam's soapbox.
这是帕姆的慷慨陈词。

1365
00:55:57.060 --> 00:56:02.280
And you guys, as an actor, when we got to have a moment where we commanded the whole bullpen,
各位，作为演员，当我们迎来一个掌控整个开放式办公区的时刻时，

1366
00:56:02.700 --> 00:56:03.580
it was exciting.
这让人很兴奋。

1367
00:56:03.580 --> 00:56:05.740
And also we were like kind of terrified.
但同时我们也觉得有点吓人。

1368
00:56:05.980 --> 00:56:06.580
Oh, yeah.
哦，是的。

1369
00:56:06.740 --> 00:56:08.740
Because you're in charge of like the pace of the scene.
因为你要负责掌控整个场景的节奏。

1370
00:56:08.740 --> 00:56:12.500
This only happened to me a handful of times when Angela makes a big announcement or something.
这种情况我只经历过几次，比如安吉拉有什么重大宣布之类的时候。

1371
00:56:12.820 --> 00:56:16.680
But I remember, Jenna, watching you and you were so good in this moment
但我记得，珍娜，我看着你，在这个时刻你表现得太棒了

1372
00:56:16.680 --> 00:56:19.680
because everyone is like throwing you little curveballs.
因为每个人都在给你抛各种小难题。

1373
00:56:19.860 --> 00:56:21.860
You know, Oscar and Stanley and Kevin.
你知道的，奥斯卡、斯坦利和凯文。

1374
00:56:22.120 --> 00:56:23.840
You know, they're all kind of sassing you.
你知道，他们都有点在对你阴阳怪气。

1375
00:56:24.000 --> 00:56:28.560
And you know, the last time that I had a scene like this was back in Beach Games
你知道，我上一次有这样的戏份还是在《海滩游戏》那一集

1376
00:56:28.560 --> 00:56:32.860
when Pam was going to confront the whole group about her feelings
当时帕姆准备向大家坦白她的感受

1377
00:56:32.860 --> 00:56:34.560
and how they didn't come to her art show.
以及他们为什么没有去看她的画展。

1378
00:56:34.700 --> 00:56:38.300
But in this instance, people were interrupting me and they're coming at me.
但在这次的事件中，人们一直在打断我，向我发起攻势。

1379
00:56:38.300 --> 00:56:42.960
And I got such a window into what Steve's every day was.
这让我深深体会到了史蒂夫每天过的是什么日子。

1380
00:56:43.420 --> 00:56:43.620
Yeah.
是啊。

1381
00:56:44.180 --> 00:56:48.900
At one point, the group starts hazing Pam about being in New York.
有一会儿，大家开始拿帕姆在纽约待过这事开涮。

1382
00:56:49.080 --> 00:56:52.900
And Pam gives this speech that kind of takes Jim off guard.
而帕姆发表了一番让吉姆有点措手不及的演讲。

1383
00:56:52.980 --> 00:56:54.560
And I think we should hear it.
我想我们应该听听看。

1384
00:56:55.060 --> 00:56:56.660
Listen, New York.
听着，纽约。

1385
00:56:56.940 --> 00:56:58.140
That might fly.
那套可能行得通。

1386
00:56:58.300 --> 00:56:58.560
Why?
为什么？

1387
00:56:58.720 --> 00:57:00.380
Because I went to New York for three months.
因为我在纽约待了三个月。

1388
00:57:00.700 --> 00:57:02.540
That and the black sweater of Manhattan.
还有那件曼哈顿黑色毛衣。

1389
00:57:02.980 --> 00:57:03.640
OK, yes.
好吧，是的。

1390
00:57:03.740 --> 00:57:05.200
I went to New York, everybody.
我去过纽约，各位。

1391
00:57:05.200 --> 00:57:07.080
I'm not going to apologize for it.
我不会为此道歉的。

1392
00:57:07.080 --> 00:57:10.860
I experienced more there in one week than I experienced here in three months.
我在那里一周经历的事情，比我在这里三个月经历的还要多。

1393
00:57:11.000 --> 00:57:11.900
I love New York.
我爱纽约。

1394
00:57:12.140 --> 00:57:15.000
You know, I especially love that people there cleaned up after themselves.
你知道，我尤其喜欢那里的人会自己收拾干净。

1395
00:57:15.440 --> 00:57:17.240
Well, Jim has just heard her say all that.
吉姆刚刚听到了她说的这一切。

1396
00:57:17.560 --> 00:57:17.760
Yeah.
是啊。

1397
00:57:17.940 --> 00:57:20.060
And the camera is pushing in on his face.
镜头正在推近他的脸。

1398
00:57:20.220 --> 00:57:25.600
And he's realizing at the end of today, he's going to tell her he bought them a house in Scranton.
他意识到在今天结束时，他要告诉她他在斯克兰顿买了一栋房子。

1399
00:57:25.600 --> 00:57:27.880
And she's not going back to New York anytime soon.
而她短时间内是不会回纽约了。

1400
00:57:28.040 --> 00:57:29.380
This place she loves.
这个她深爱的地方。

1401
00:57:29.640 --> 00:57:35.520
I really wish this moment had made it into the show because I feel like it just sets up the stakes for Jim.
我真的很希望这一幕能剪进正片里，因为我觉得它为吉姆奠定了情感基调。

1402
00:57:35.760 --> 00:57:38.580
Because he's doubting his decision from the very beginning.
因为他从一开始就在质疑自己的决定。

1403
00:57:38.720 --> 00:57:39.540
Did I do the right thing?
我做得对吗？

1404
00:57:39.580 --> 00:57:40.460
Is she going to like this?
她会喜欢这个吗？

1405
00:57:40.500 --> 00:57:41.040
I don't know.
我不知道。

1406
00:57:41.220 --> 00:57:43.120
And I feel like he needed to hear this.
而且我觉得他需要听到这些。

1407
00:57:43.200 --> 00:57:45.140
And I feel like the audience needed to hear it.
而且我觉得观众也需要听到这些。

1408
00:57:45.280 --> 00:57:45.720
I do, too.
我也这么觉得。

1409
00:57:45.780 --> 00:57:47.280
I think it's a shame that it got cut out.
我觉得被剪掉太可惜了。

1410
00:57:47.280 --> 00:57:53.080
And, you know, at the end of this whole scene, Pam says, fine, I'll go clean it.
而且，你知道的，在这场戏的最后，帕姆说，好吧，我去清理。

1411
00:57:53.300 --> 00:57:57.240
So it is Pam, in the end, who cleaned the microwave.
所以到头来，清理微波炉的人还是帕姆。

1412
00:57:57.940 --> 00:57:58.180
Yes.
是的。

1413
00:57:58.300 --> 00:58:02.840
In the script, the very last line of this big scene says this.
在剧本里，这场重头戏的最后一句台词是这样的。

1414
00:58:03.100 --> 00:58:08.140
Pam marches over to the kitchen and Stanley starts to slow clap.
帕姆走向厨房，斯坦利开始带头缓慢鼓掌。

1415
00:58:10.190 --> 00:58:10.710
Oh, yeah.
哦，对。

1416
00:58:11.250 --> 00:58:12.950
We had a slow clap.
我们有过缓慢鼓掌的戏份。

1417
00:58:15.000 --> 00:58:16.400
Oh, yeah, that's right.
哦，对，没错。

1418
00:58:16.580 --> 00:58:20.280
Oh, that's bringing back that memory of me walking to Stanley's slow clap.
哦，这勾起了我走向斯坦利缓慢鼓掌时的记忆。

1419
00:58:20.800 --> 00:58:21.720
Mm-hmm.
嗯哼。

1420
00:58:22.640 --> 00:58:23.580
So good.
太棒了。

1421
00:58:23.960 --> 00:58:24.640
So good.
太棒了。

1422
00:58:25.280 --> 00:58:32.200
It's time for Michael to plant what he thinks is two pounds of marijuana in Toby's desk.
接下来轮到迈克尔把自以为有两磅的大麻藏进托比的办公桌里。

1423
00:58:32.440 --> 00:58:41.300
And at the same time, Dwight is going to call the police and report that there is a drug dealer named Toby Flunderson on the premises.
与此同时，德懷特要报警，举报说大楼里有个叫托比·弗伦德森的毒贩。

1424
00:58:41.600 --> 00:58:45.260
And when asked to give his name, Dwight says his name is Andy Bernard.
当被问及姓名时，德懷特说他的名字叫安迪·伯纳德。

1425
00:58:45.620 --> 00:58:48.800
Dwight is going to throw Andy under the bus any chance he gets.
德懷特只要有机会就会毫不犹豫地出卖安迪。

1426
00:58:48.800 --> 00:58:56.940
There was this deleted scene, Jenna, that for Michael to be able to have the time to go plant the drugs, they needed to get Toby away from his desk.
詹娜，曾经有一个被删掉的片段，为了让迈克尔有时间去藏毒，他们需要把托比调离座位。

1427
00:58:57.280 --> 00:59:01.320
So Dwight asked Toby to show him his photos from Costa Rica.
所以德懷特让托比把哥斯达黎加的照片给他看。

1428
00:59:01.500 --> 00:59:02.780
Let's go to the conference room.
我们去会议室吧。

1429
00:59:02.920 --> 00:59:03.940
I'll look at your photos.
我来看你的照片。

1430
00:59:04.320 --> 00:59:06.840
Toby is thrilled that someone wants to see his photos.
托比一听有人想看他的照片，高兴坏了。

1431
00:59:07.180 --> 00:59:09.580
And then Michael sneaks off to plant the drugs.
然后迈克尔偷偷溜去藏毒。

1432
00:59:09.580 --> 00:59:13.800
But in true Michael fashion, he can't keep the secret.
但延续了迈克尔一贯的作风，他根本守不住秘密。

1433
00:59:14.040 --> 00:59:17.260
He has to share with someone that he might have just done something.
他必须跟别人分享自己刚刚可能干了一件大事。

1434
00:59:17.500 --> 00:59:18.480
This is what he said.
他是这么说的。

1435
00:59:19.200 --> 00:59:22.000
I think it's really cool that you wanted to see my photos.
我觉得你想看我的照片真的很酷。

1436
00:59:22.300 --> 00:59:22.860
What's this for?
这个是什么？

1437
00:59:22.880 --> 00:59:24.100
Pink thing on that white oval.
白色椭圆上那个粉红色的东西。

1438
00:59:24.200 --> 00:59:24.560
That's me.
那是我。

1439
00:59:24.680 --> 00:59:25.480
I was boogie boarding.
我在冲浪板上冲浪。

1440
00:59:25.780 --> 00:59:26.000
Wait.
等等。

1441
00:59:26.560 --> 00:59:27.740
Who took this picture?
这张照片是谁拍的？

1442
00:59:27.980 --> 00:59:28.900
Did you make some friends?
你交到朋友了吗？

1443
00:59:29.520 --> 00:59:34.340
Oh, so I hired a local kid to snap it.
哦，我雇了个当地小孩抓拍的。

1444
00:59:34.880 --> 00:59:35.700
Tell me about this monkey.
跟我讲讲这只猴子的事吧。

1445
00:59:38.450 --> 00:59:41.170
Oh, okay.
